-- M7 s5 (O17, D11): a well-typed hint whose value traps. The hint v is the
-- Field fold of the identity step at a Nat sum that overflows, thus the
-- fold computes to a trap (SPEC.md 9, O17). langc check gives ok, and langc
-- circuit gives the IR, because the lowering does not evaluate a hint.
-- langc witness evaluates the hint and gives WITNESS_HINT (exit 1) with no
-- file (test/circuit/refuse.txt). The circuit hintTrap has no golden.
def badField : Field := fold (fun (y : Field) => y) 0 (natAdd 18446744073709551615 1)

circuit hintTrap private (x : Field) hint v := badField := v == x
